Removes the landing rule from `FolderState::scanned` (f53c1de), which
leaves `land` unused: an occupant at a marked path that matches what the
path's want or a deferred carrier was committing is no longer adopted
with a new `seq`. The mark is cleared and the occupant is observed like
any file; when it matches the restored record the index is left as it
is, so a refetch whose report a crash took keeps that record's old
`seq`, is never announced, and the peers this machine refused before it
landed never ask again (DESIGN.md §8.3 step 2, §13).

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_restores_landing_is_announced_to_peers_it_refused
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::an_occupant_matching_the_restored_record_is_the_landing
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::an_occupant_matching_a_later_carrier_is_its_landing

